WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.980
When the minister saw Tom walking forward to receive the Bible, he was shocked.

2
00:00:04.981 --> 00:00:09.804
The minister could not imagine how Tom had mastered two thousand lines of verse.

3
00:00:09.805 --> 00:00:12.388
But the boys and girls sitting there knew.

4
00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:17.134
They had sold their tickets for the sake of Tom's glory.

5
00:00:17.135 --> 00:00:22.139
After Tom received his Bible, he was introduced to the judge, the new girl's father.

6
00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:25.009
"What's your name?" asked the judge.

7
00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:30.666
"T-T-Tom-T-Thomas," stuttered a very nervous Tom.

8
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:35.706
"You're a fine boy, Thomas, and two thousand verses is a lot of verses.

9
00:00:35.707 --> 00:00:39.386
You won't be sorry you learned them," said the judge.

10
00:00:39.387 --> 00:00:44.490
Tom thought he was free to go, but then the judge continued, "Knowledge is precious.

11
00:00:44.491 --> 00:00:48.973
It's what makes good men great, and I can see you'll be a great man.

12
00:00:48.974 --> 00:00:55.106
I'm sure you know the names of all of Jesus' disciples, but who were his first two disciples?"

13
00:00:55.107 --> 00:01:00.210
Tom was uncertain if he was supposed to answer, so he remained quiet.

14
00:01:00.211 --> 00:01:04.077
"Thomas, answer the question," the minister prodded him.

15
00:01:04.078 --> 00:01:10.279
At that, Tom shouted out the only two names from the Bible he could remember, "David and Goliath!"

16
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.037
The church erupted into laughter. Tom slunk back to his seat.

17
00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:20.144
His aunt poked him angrily.

18
00:01:20.145 --> 00:01:25.006
The next morning Tom woke up knowing it was Monday, and Monday meant school.

19
00:01:25.007 --> 00:01:29.777
Tom hated school more than he hated work, and this Monday was no different.

20
00:01:29.778 --> 00:01:34.537
He was feeling especially sheepish after his fall from grace at the church.

21
00:01:34.538 --> 00:01:40.918
But at school he would see the new girl. School would be bearable.

22
00:01:40.919 --> 00:01:44.374
On the way to school, Tom met his friend Huck.

23
00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:50.587
Huck's father was a drunk, so Huck was the only boy in town who didn't have to go to church or school.

24
00:01:50.588 --> 00:01:55.883
"Hey, Huck," said Tom. He noticed that his friend was holding something.

25
00:01:55.884 --> 00:01:57.734
"What have you got?"

26
00:01:57.735 --> 00:02:01.121
"Something that will cure warts," said Huck.

27
00:02:01.122 --> 00:02:04.616
"I have lots of warts," said Tom.

28
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:09.365
"Come with me to the graveyard tonight, and I can get rid of them for you," said Huck.

29
00:02:09.366 --> 00:02:11.848
Tom thought that was a good idea.

30
00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:16.590
Tom and Huck said good-bye, and Tom continued walking to school.

31
00:02:16.591 --> 00:02:21.019
By the time Tom finally got to school, he was late.

32
00:02:21.020 --> 00:02:24.924
"Where have you been?" the teacher asked.

33
00:02:24.925 --> 00:02:30.652
Tom usually made up a story when he was late. But today was different.

34
00:02:30.653 --> 00:02:36.295
If he told the teacher the truth, he would be punished by being made to sit with the girls.

35
00:02:36.296 --> 00:02:39.851
He saw that the only empty seat was beside the new girl.

36
00:02:39.852 --> 00:02:42.652
His punishment would be to sit next to her!

37
00:02:42.653 --> 00:02:46.954
"I was talking with Huckleberry Finn," answered Tom.

38
00:02:46.955 --> 00:02:49.106
The teacher was shocked.

39
00:02:49.107 --> 00:02:54.098
"Thomas Sawyer! That boy is bad, and you should not talk with bad boys."

40
00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:58.027
Tom apologized, and the teacher made him sit next to the new girl.

41
00:02:58.028 --> 00:03:02.900
Tom saw the winks and heard the whispers of the other boys and girls, but he didn't care.

42
00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:06.906
He was happy that his plan had worked, and he pretended to read.

43
00:03:06.907 --> 00:03:09.942
Tom put a peach on the new girl's desk.

44
00:03:09.943 --> 00:03:15.794
Tom then wrote on his slate, "Please take it. I have more."

45
00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:19.680
The girl read the slate and quickly looked away.

46
00:03:19.681 --> 00:03:26.074
Soon Tom began to draw, and with his left hand, he hid what he was drawing.

47
00:03:26.075 --> 00:03:29.768
"Let me see," the girl whispered.

48
00:03:29.769 --> 00:03:34.334
"I wish I could draw," she said when Tom finally showed her.

49
00:03:34.335 --> 00:03:36.776
"It's easy," said Tom.

50
00:03:36.777 --> 00:03:41.185
"Stay for lunch and I'll teach you. What's your name?"

51
00:03:41.186 --> 00:03:45.145
"I'm Becky Thatcher. What's your . . . Oh, I know.

52
00:03:45.146 --> 00:03:48.735
I remember you from church. You're Thomas Sawyer."

53
00:03:48.736 --> 00:03:55.235
"They only call me that when I'm bad," said Tom. "You can call me Tom."

54
00:03:55.236 --> 00:03:59.560
Tom wrote some words on his slate, and again he hid them from Becky.

55
00:03:59.561 --> 00:04:04.565
She begged to see them. Tom whispered: "Promise you won't tell."

56
00:04:04.566 --> 00:04:13.048
"I promise," said Becky. Tom moved his hand, and Becky read the words: "'I love you.' Oh, you're bad!"

57
00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:19.825
She blushed and turned away, but Tom saw her smiling, and he knew she was pleased.

58
00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:25.112
At lunch Tom and Becky met behind the schoolhouse, and Tom asked Becky a question.

59
00:04:25.113 --> 00:04:27.495
"Have you ever been engaged?"

60
00:04:27.496 --> 00:04:30.136
"No," replied Becky.

61
00:04:30.137 --> 00:04:33.009
"Would you like to be?" asked Tom.

62
00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.614
"Maybe. What's special about it?"

63
00:04:36.615 --> 00:04:43.737
"Well," said Tom, "first we kiss, and then you only like me, and I only like you.

64
00:04:43.738 --> 00:04:46.790
And we walk to and from school together."

65
00:04:46.791 --> 00:04:52.108
Becky thought it sounded nice, so she said, "I love you," in Tom's ear.

66
00:04:52.109 --> 00:04:56.175
"I never thought I'd be engaged," said Becky smiling.

67
00:04:56.176 --> 00:05:00.820
"It's fun," said Tom. "Amy and I—"

68
00:05:00.821 --> 00:05:10.286
"Oh, Tom, you've been engaged before!" shouted Becky, and she began to cry.

69
00:05:10.287 --> 00:05:15.415
Tom tried to comfort her, but she wouldn't listen. She was hurt and angry.

70
00:05:15.416 --> 00:05:23.044
"I only care for you!" said Tom, and he left.

